From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: File › Print holds only printing, Print first and primary, labelled odd/even list; Recover and account tip translated; no placeholder user name

WP23 usability finding (docs/phase4/design-system.md 1.1 #4 and the name leaks): File › Print shared its function with Export, so the page ended with eleven "save a copy" buttons; the odd/even list had no label and read as a second page list; Print and "Save these pages as PDF…" were two equal buttons below the printer; Print Markup sat above everything; three settings, the Recover page and the title bar's account tip were English in every language. Print now has its own page in the app's own widgets: Print (accent, primary) and Save as PDF first, then the printer and copies, Pages with a labelled "Odd or even pages" list, Orientation, Scale to paper size, Print Markup and the page count; the formats stay on File › Export. The missing Russian rows go into ru.tsv (the suite catalog carries the Uzbek ones). Upstream's placeholder user name "WordCraft User" is replaced by the system account's name until Options sets one, as Word takes the Windows user's (not in tests; the web has no account name and keeps it).
